# Git workflow

This standing instruction is the ask. Do not wait for another "commit" or "open a PR." `origin` is `https://github.com/tambykojak/tks-addon-manager`. The old name redirects.

## Start

Before the first edit:

1. Fetch `origin`. If this folder is on a clean `main`, pull.
2. A new agent runs `git checkout -b BRANCH_NAME origin/main`. That creates the branch and checks it out. `BRANCH_NAME` is `addon/<name>/<short>`, `tkam/<short>`, `web/<short>`, or `fix/<short>`.
3. Then run `git push -fu origin HEAD` or `git push -fu origin BRANCH_NAME`. The new branch must be on the remote.
4. Edit on that branch.

A question or a plan does not get a branch. A change that spans turns stays on its branch. Unrelated addon, site, and app work each get their own branch.

If the folder has uncommitted work that is not this change, stop. Do not switch off a branch that has uncommitted work.

## Ship

Once a change is made:

1. Commit on the branch. The subject is imperative and says why, in one or two sentences: `Sell grey junk in one vendor pass.`
2. Rebase onto `origin/main` when the branch is behind. If the rebase conflicts, stop and name the files.
3. Push with `git push -fu origin HEAD`. If a pull request is not already created, create it in draft. The title matches the commit. The body says what a player or the app can do now, and how to check it.

Do not merge a change that is unfinished.

## Parallel agents

Two agents do not both edit `Common/`, `Libs/`, `Scripts/`, `TKAM/`, `Web/`, or the same addon. The one that finishes second rebases onto `origin/main`. An overlap stays on its branch.

## Still ask first

- Do not bump `VERSION` or create a `tkam-v*` tag unless asked. A player-facing addon change still includes its `RELEASE.md` note, using the version already in `Main.lua`.
- Do not force-push `main`, hard-reset, or skip hooks.
- Leave out secrets, signing keys, `node_modules`, Rust `target`, `dist`, and Terraform state.

`TKAM/` or `Web/` needs `npm install` before you run it. An addon change does not. If the push fails, stop and say what blocked it.
